%N A398244 Array read by antidiagonals: T(n,k) is the number of feedback vertex sets in the grid graph P_n X P_k.
%C A398244 Equivalently, T(n,k) is the number of acyclic induced subgraphs in P_n X P_k. The complement of an acyclic induced subgraph is a feedback vertex set.
%C A398244 All rows and columns are linear recurrences with constant coefficients. The maximum order of the recursions is given in A398248.
%H A398244 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A398244/b398244.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..629</a> (first 35 antidiagonals)
%H A398244 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/FeedbackVertexSetNumber.html">Feedback Vertex Set Number</a>.
%H A398244 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/GridGraph.html">Grid Graph</a>.
%F A398244 T(n,k) = T(k,n).
